    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the mass of a 100 kg sample of uranium-232 after 20 years? Round to the nearest kilogram.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Approximately 82 kg.",
          "worked": "Use $M_0=100$, $H=68.9$ and $t=20$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}M&=100\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{\\frac{20}{68.9}}\\,\\mathrm{kg}\\\\M&\\approx82\\,\\mathrm{kg}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How long will it take for a 100 kg sample of uranium-232 to decay to less than 10 kg? Round to the nearest year.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "229 years to the nearest year.\n\nFind when the mass reaches 10 kg. It is below 10 kg after that time.",
          "worked": "Let $T$ be the time in years when the mass reaches 10 kg.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}100\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{\\frac{T}{68.9}}&=10\\\\\\left(\\frac12\\right)^{\\frac{T}{68.9}}&=\\frac1{10}\\\\\\frac{T}{68.9}\\ln\\!\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=\\ln\\!\\left(\\frac1{10}\\right)\\\\T&=68.9\\frac{\\ln 10}{\\ln 2}\\\\T&\\approx228.88\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe mass decreases with time, so it is less than 10 kg when $t>T$. This gives 229 years to the nearest year.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
